>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be at least 1-D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (zero-th dimension index must be valid to flip along up/down)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : i = 0
>>
Rule 3 (for tensors with at least 1-D, each dimension size is non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0 else false
>>
Rule 4 (scalar tensors are not allowed)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) > 1
